WEBVTT

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.580
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.060
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed, do they want to protect themselves or other people.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.780
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.720
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.350
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.460
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.770
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.460
Ken, ken, pa! {this is hopscotch}

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.860
Ken, ken, pa!

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.520
Ken, ken, pa!

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.240
Hey!

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.950
Ken, ken, pa!

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:09.380
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.880
and the listed sponsors.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.840
It was really interesting!

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.370
Not, really?

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.920
You should’ve come too!

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.490
But…

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.200
Jigoku Shoujo?

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.760
Get out of the way.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.770
It’s pointless even if you go.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.100
Get out of the way!

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.400
Your grudge is received.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.320
Good morning.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:54.600
Oh, Nawa, do you know where Nakajima is?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.450
What?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.240
He wasn’t in the dorms.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.880
With no evidence of waking up.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:02.670
Since you were close, we were wondering
 if you knew anything.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:05.550
I dunno.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.090
Really?

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.840
If you hear anything, tell the manager.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.650
Sure.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.680
Nawa!

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:32.370
Tonight, we’re going drinking with
 my girlfriend’s girlfriends,

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.620
but do you want to come too?

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.360
It’s truthfully a Goukon.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:38.120
Note: Goukon means, a drinking party with members of the opposite sex, as a match-up thing.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.120
You should join us sometimes.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.830
Since there’s an imbalance in the number of people. {meaning male/female ratio}

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:43.170
No, I’m not good at those.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.600
What? He’s so unsociable.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:52.340
Maybe he has <i>those</i> interests. {meaning homosexual?}

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.400
Big brother! {well, it’s onii-chan, but they’re not actually related}

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:01.840
Kayo-chan!

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:08.180
You stink like oil!

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:10.370
I won’t play with you!

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:18.220
Sorry as always, Nawa-san.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:20.870
No, I just like children.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:24.130
You don’t like children, you like Kayo, right?

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:26.870
I guess so.

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:33.050
Ken, ken, pa!

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:36.260
Ken, ken, pa!

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.720
Ken, ken, pa!

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.740
Are you OK?

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.200
Once more!

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.730
Treated like a lolicon at his workplace, eh?

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.720
Ken, ken, pa!

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:50.490
A youngster of good age, playing with little girls, that’s…

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:55.230
Even though in the past, looking with such eyes was weirder. {as in, before there wouldn’t have been such understanding}

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:57.430
That’s called eras, right?

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:00.620
Ken, ken, pa!

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:02.370
Ken, ken…

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:32.660
Starting office work today, this is Miyajima Yuki.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:35.580
Everyone, nice to meet you.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:44.410
Nakajima-san still hasn’t contacted us.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.080
He quit, didn’t he?

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.200
Can’t he resign officially?

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:54.150
There are lots of youngsters like that with no common sense whatsoever!

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.460
Miyajima-san!

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:03.410
Please will you go out with me? Only once!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:05.780
Um, these sort of things are troublesome.

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:11.530
When young and beautiful women like you come, our company has better credibility!

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.870
I mean, all the women here are old?

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:15.060
So, come on…

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:19.780
Two hours, drinking and laughing is all I ask, right?

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.510
I’m sorry, I’m very sorry.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.230
Thank you very much. I’ve been saved!

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.780
Not, really…

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:45.560
Can I buy you dinner as a token of my gratitude?

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:48.170
How about the one in front of the station?

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:51.390
Sorry, I have a commitment today already.

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:52.810
Big brother!

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.500
Today’s hide-and-seek, OK?

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.520
Yup, I know.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:04.560
Well then, see you later!

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:05.780
Sure.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.020
A commitment…?

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.010
Yes.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.130
You like children, don’t you?

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:18.030
Then tomorrow, can I buy you lunch?

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.780
You’re OK with that, right?

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.050
Sure.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:37.410
Nawa-san, you don’t speak at all, do you?

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.160
Sorry.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.860
Then can I ask you something?

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.660
How old are you?

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:45.860
Twenty seven.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.480
Where are you from?

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.710
Saitama.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:49.840
Hobby?

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:51.850
None, really.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:53.040
Girlfriend?

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.120
None.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.270
What do you do after going home?

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:03.250
I feel like I understand what you’re like.

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.780
A boring person.

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:08.910
But it’s relaxing when I’m with you.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:12.300
Since you’re not glaring like the others.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:14.760
Oh, really?

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:21.780
Can you tell me about the factory, since it’s awkward asking someone else?

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:23.980
S-Sure,

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:25.290
if you’re fine with me.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.840
This is my friend, Kikuri-chan.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.690
It doesn’t seem like he remembers me.

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:31.680
Big brother, you seem happy!

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:34.560
Did something good happen to you?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.420
No, nothing really.

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:39.790
You like that girl, don’t you?

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:45.690
Looks like you’ve finally noticed.

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:49.990
It’s true, right?

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:53.290
If you’re too impudent, I won’t play with you!

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.290
What’s this?

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.880
It’s a bruise I’ve had for a while.

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.300
Was it there before?

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.120
Was it?

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.130
Was it?

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.610
You haven’t eaten dinner yet, have you?

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:41.900
Your knife is rusty. You should use it occasionally.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:48.590
Nawa-san, I heard you were good friends with someone named Nakajima-san.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.240
What? No, not that good.

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:54.600
But you apparently played with Kayo and him.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:56.370
Occasionally.

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:58.920
Has he not contacted you?

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:01.470
Everyone’s troubled because he’s missing.

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:02.290
Um…

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:02.850
What?

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:06.460
Could you stop things like this?

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:08.740
What do you mean?

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:12.610
I’m glad, and it’s not that bothersome.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:15.130
But, I’ve been through a lot.

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:19.630
What’s “a lot”?

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:24.920
To get to the point, I have no right
 for you to treat me like this.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.230
Can you go home?

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:29.430
You’re very one-sided, aren’t you?

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:30.870
Sorry.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.590
Can’t you tell me what the situation is?

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:37.380
If I’m satisfied, I’ll go home.

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:39.360
Even if I told you, you wouldn’t believe me.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.850
I’d have to hear it first to know if that’s true!

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.870
Do you know about Jigoku Shoujo?

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.020
Jigoku Shoujo?

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:52.610
I just heard about her in stories.

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:56.650
That by accessing the Hell Correspondence at midnight,

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:59.660
and submitting the name of who you hate,

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:02.810
Jigoku Shoujo will ferry that person to Hell.

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:06.290
But it was true.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:12.890
When I submitted someone’s name, thinking about myself, I was able to meet Jigoku Shoujo.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.290
Someone?

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.530
That was Nakajima.

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:21.850
<i>Hello!</i>

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:25.620
<i>Looks like you’re having fun!</i>

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:29.320
Nakajima, right after joining the factory, got closer to us.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:35.650
He felt a bit shady,

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:39.190
but Kayo-chan wasn’t suspecting anything,

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:42.220
we started playing all together.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.890
<i>Good! It’s a cute picture.</i>

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.190
<i>What a weird face!</i>

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:58.560
I felt something different in Nakajima.

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:15.330
One day, I sneaked into Nakajima’s room and searched it.

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:24.270
That came out.

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:33.130
There were some quite risqué photos.

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:38.700
I was convinced that he had those kind of interest.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:43.070
<i>Nakajima, what did you do?!</i>

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:45.400
<i>I’m just taking them. I don’t plan on advancing on her.</i>

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.400
<i>That’s not the issue here!</i>

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.090
<i>I’m fortunate just watching her.</i>

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.600
<i>What will happen to her, with that force put onto her?</i>

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:55.330
<i>I don’t know, since she’s just a child.</i>

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:59.160
<i>Don’t get too excited. Aren’t you the same?</i>

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.370
<i>Don’t equate us!</i>

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:07.430
<i>If you do anything more, I’ll tell everyone we’re the same.</i>

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.220
<i>Be quiet for me.</i>

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.800
<i>I’m not about to cross the line.</i>

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:23.390
That moment, I remembered the rumor about Jigoku Shoujo.

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:29.010
Curse someone, and two holes are created.

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:32.170
Apparently you too fall to Hell.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.290
But I didn’t care about that.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:37.020
I wanted to protect Kayo-chan.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:38.330
So…

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:44.540
So I’m a person destined to go to Hell.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:48.200
Such a man deserves this.

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:50.930
I can’t ever repay you.

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:12.840
After last night, I was thinking about many things.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:15.860
What you did, what you said, and many other things.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.200
And I thought…

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:23.950
…people going to Hell can be fortunate, too!

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:25.030
But…

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:30.950
Look at Kayo-chan, she looks so fortunate when she plays with you.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:34.330
You still have the power to make lives fortunate.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.830
Miyajima-san…

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:41.610
Would you like to live a life with me?

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:43.550
Life from now on.

00:18:57.310 --> 00:18:58.810
You’re late today!

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:02.310
I’m sorry, Kayo-chan. I can’t play today.

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:03.490
Why?

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:05.980
I’ve got an important appointment.

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:07.330
With that girl?

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:09.830
Yeah.

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:15.370
Well, that’s a pity. I’ll give up today.

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:16.860
Tomorrow, for sure!

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.340
Yeah, it’s a promise.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.210
Welcome.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:34.830
I’ll make some tea now, so feel at home.

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:36.350
OK.

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:06.710
He was my senior in high school.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:11.390
We were dating ever since graduating from high school.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:14.890
I was startled after hearing his interest,

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:20.900
but when we were together, that didn’t matter.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:24.400
We were a good match, you know?

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:26.420
Y-You are…

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:30.100
He wasn’t someone to suddenly go missing.

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:33.050
I told the police too, but they didn’t listen.

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:36.900
I thought I had to do something myself.

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:39.300
So I joined the factory.

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:44.650
Since I heard you were close to him, I wanted to ask you about him,

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:46.920
but I’m glad it went well.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:49.430
Did you trick me?

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:52.890
I loved him.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:55.210
For him, I would do anything.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:04.970
Did you grow to love me?

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.350
I’ll make you fall from the top to Hell.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.940
S-Stop!

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:21.920
The future…

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.210
…of that person…

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:29.220
Hate, hated, and someone else is hated.

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:34.220
Ferry, ferried, and someone else is ferried.

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:38.130
I’ve seen this repetition countless times.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:41.370
No one can stop it.

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:42.230
But…

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:44.850
But someone has to stop it!

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.230
That…

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:48.710
That’s wrong!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:52.940
That man has pulled the string already.

00:21:54.440 --> 00:22:00.540
But I might be able to stop that woman
 from ferrying him to Hell!

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:03.530
I can still make it in time!

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.000
Get out of the way!

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:10.260
Do what you like.

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:49.880
Note: Candle says,  Nawa Akihiro.

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:49.880
I will release your hatred.

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:23.910
Yes, a long time ago,

00:24:23.910 --> 00:24:25.960
I was that person’s child.

00:24:26.640 --> 00:24:29.950
I don’t remember how long ago that was.

00:24:30.580 --> 00:24:32.570
I just wanted to know…

00:24:33.180 --> 00:24:36.170
…what humans are like.

00:24:37.100 --> 00:24:38.880
Welcome home, Hikaru.

00:24:40.140 --> 00:24:42.800
And I realized…

00:24:42.800 --> 00:24:44.900
…what separation is.

00:24:45.220 --> 00:24:48.190
Next time: In the Straw.

00:24:50.730 --> 00:24:55.790
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:24:55.790 --> 00:24:58.900
and the listed sponsors.
